    <h2>About Badminton</h2>

    <p>
        Badminton is a racket sport played using a racket and a shuttlecock.
        Players hit the shuttlecock over a net and try to make it land inside
        the opponent's court.
    </p>

    <p>
        Badminton can be played as singles, where two players compete against
        each other, or doubles, where four players compete in two teams.
    </p>


    <h2>Basic Rules of Badminton</h2>

    <ol>
        <li>A badminton match can be played in singles or doubles.</li>
        <li>Players hit the shuttlecock over the net.</li>
        <li>A rally ends when the shuttlecock lands outside the court.</li>
        <li>A game is generally played to 21 points.</li>
        <li>A player or team must win by 2 points when the score reaches 20-20.</li>
    </ol>


